# THE PULSE — a smith above Cody, on a tick

*Owner-commissioned. The idea, in the owner's shape: Mineflayer is the
body, Baritone-class pathfinding is the muscle, and above them a
higher mind — Voyager-pattern — that does not play directly. It ticks
(the pulse), reads what the world did to its pupil, and writes better
scripts for the lower level. Scripts earn their place by surviving
the world, judged by referees (evidence), never by their author.*

## The machine

```
                 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   every ~10 min │  SMITH (smith.js)                             │
   + on FAIL ───►│  reads state+evidence+ledger+logs, calls the  │
                 │  presence brain THROUGH THE GOVERNOR          │
                 │  (identity league-pulse-smith) for ONE        │
                 │  artefact: a skill script or a revision       │
                 └──────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                                ▼ candidate (library/, header sidecar)
                 ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                 │  TRIAL GATE (trial.js)                        │
                 │  fresh Cody relaunch on [promoted…, candidate]│
                 │  bounded window; verdict ONLY from evidence:  │
                 │  state-feed inventories, block scans, deaths, │
                 │  the Orin server log → ledger.jsonl           │
                 └──────┬───────────────────────┬───────────────┘
                   PASS ▼                       ▼ FAIL
             promoted (active.json)     stays in library, marked;
                                        the smith reads it next tick
                                ▼
   CODY (resident-cody.js + pulse-plugin.js) runs the promoted set
   on loop in the world: state feed every 10 s, evidence scan every
   30 s, deaths appended to deaths.jsonl, project narration injected
   into his brain via the framework's prompt-fragment path.
```

## Pieces

- `pulse-plugin.js` — plugin passed to `createBot` via
  `options.plugins` (the framework's own idiom; **no framework source
  was modified**). State feed, skill runner, evidence scan
  (flood-fill shelter judge), narration fragment, death log.
- `lib/prims.js` — **SEEDED PRIMITIVES, hand-written by the scaffold
  author and declared as such.** Timeout-guarded mineflayer helpers
  (goto, dig, craft, place, chest I/O) that smith scripts compose.
  They are the workbench, not the work. Everything the curriculum is
  *judged* on is written by the smith.
- `smith.js` — the tick. Its prompt's API surface is extracted from
  the real source at runtime (`src/actions/index.js` descriptions,
  `// prim:` lines, `node_modules/mineflayer/docs/api.md` sections) —
  never from an operator's memory. Candidates are `node --check`ed
  and shape-tested in a child process before storage.
- `trial.js` — the gate. `run --stage Sx --candidate <file>` and
  `night` (the S5 watch). Kills and relaunches Cody; NEVER restarts
  the Minecraft server (server restarts kill Cody's reconnect — hard
  lesson from the headed-world session).
- `curriculum.json` — the settle-in exam: S1 gather+tools → S2 stone
  → S3 shelter → S4 furnish → S5 one full night inside, zero deaths.
  Each stage names the evidence its verdict is computed from.
- `resident-cody.js` patch (in `bots/runs/cody/`, `.orig` kept):
  two touches — pass the pulse plugin to `createBot`, and the wander
  loop steps aside while the skill runner is active
  (`global.__pulseRunnerActive`).

## Trust discipline (non-negotiable)

- A candidate never silently becomes Cody. Promotion happens only in
  `trial.js`, only on PASS, and the verdict cites its evidence.
- Rollback = relaunch Cody on the previous active set. Always cheap,
  always available.
- Mind-spend flows only through the governor and is receipted in
  `ledger/mind-calls.jsonl` under `league-cody` / `league-pulse-smith`.
- If the brain's scripts prove too weak after several ticks, that is
  a finding to report with the failed artefacts — not a licence to
  hand-write curriculum scripts. (Seeded primitives above are the one
  declared exception.)

