## Build log - 2026-11-07 (resident mind-link, fault 2: CLOSED)

- **The differing variable: `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` — the
  absence of `Content-Length`.** Wire capture (echo listener,
  `pulse/bisect/cap-client.raw` vs `cap-fetch.raw`): the league
  `LLMClient` (raw Node `http.request`, body via `req.write`) sends
  its POST with `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` and no Content-Length.
  Every working client (Vega, Geist, the smith — all Node `fetch`;
  curl) sends a `Content-Length`. Cody's resident is the only
  chunked client in the league.
- **Mechanism (two governor defects compounding):**
  `proxy/governor.py` read the request body only when a
  Content-Length header was present, so a chunked body was silently
  dropped (`body = b""` — hence `model: null` on all six 502
  receipts). Its header-copy loop then forwarded the client's
  `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` upstream (not in the skip list)
  together with `Content-Length: 0` and no body at all, so
  llama-server waited for chunk frames that could never arrive
  until the governor's 300 s upstream cap fired. Six attempts, six
  502s at 300.0 s, ~1800 mind-seconds charged to Cody.
- **Bisect table** (governor replays, throwaway identities, brain
  untouched):
  | rung | shape | identity | result |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | A | Content-Length (curl control) | bisect-a | 200 in 0.181 s, receipted |
  | B | chunked (curl, LLMClient shape) | bisect-b | no response in 25 s (hang reproduced; its 502 receipt was lost when the old governor process was stopped for the fix — the hang lived in that process) |
  | C | chunked, after the governor fix | bisect-c | 200 in 0.195 s, receipted, model + tokens parsed |
- **Fixes (both ours, backups kept):**
  1. `proxy/governor.py` (backup `governor.py.bak-chunked-20261107`):
     `_forward` now de-chunks a chunked request body
     (`_read_chunked`) instead of dropping it, and
     `transfer-encoding` is stripped from the headers forwarded
     upstream; the true Content-Length of the de-chunked body is
     set as before. `py_compile` clean. The governor was restarted
     to load the fix (pid 2141516 -> 2294325). **Recorded side
     effect:** the restart clears the governor's in-memory rolling
     budget windows for every agent (the ledger receipts persist);
     Cody's 1800 mind-second lockout cleared with them. That was
     not the purpose of the restart — the fix cannot load without
     one — but it is the fact, so it is written here.
  2. `bots/craftmind/src/brain.js` (backup
     `brain.js.bak-chunked-20261107`): `LLMClient._callAPI` now
     sends `Content-Length: Buffer.byteLength(body)`, so the
     resident speaks fixed-length to any proxy, not only to a
     de-chunking one. `node --check` clean. The resident was
     relaunched via `codyctl.py` (pid 2273124 -> 2295830) to load
     it; clean boot, greeting posted, deaths unchanged.
